==Etymology==
An eon is a time measurement unit that involves multiple eras and is equal to one billion years.

==Trivia==
[[File:2Race (304).png|Omnitrix Silhouette|thumb]]

*Eon's working name was Ben/Eon and supposed to speak in Ben and Eon's voices cobbled together.{{Refn|[[:File:HoA 59.png]]|group=script}}<ref>'''''[[Ben 10 and the Hands of Armageddon]]'''''</ref>
*Eon was originally canon to the [[Prime Timeline]] as of the first season on '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]'''.{{Refn|[[:File:RAT Originally Canon.PNG]]|group=DM}}
** Because he is no longer canon to the Prime Timeline, Eon is one of two regular transformations that has never been used by [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Prime]] on-screen, the other being [[Spitter]].
*The [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] turned violet when displaying Eon's silhouette as his [[Eon|original counterpart]] embedded his consciousness into the DNA sample.{{Refn|[[:File:Eon Retain Personality.png]]|name=source|group = pop-up}}<ref name="RAT" />
*Eon was the second alien form that has managed to repress [[Ben Tennyson (Race Against Time Timeline)|Ben]]'s personality, the first being [[Ghostfreak]].{{Refn|group = pop-up|name = Beon}}<ref name="RAT" />
*[[Duncan Rouleau]] believes that Eon still exists as a transformation for an alternate version of Ben in the [[Multiverse]],{{Refn|[[:File:Eon Transformation Exists in the Multiverse.png]]|name=eonexists|group = DR}} thus implying that the [[Chronian|Chronians]] do exist in specific universes.
**Duncan also believes that Ben could have had full control over Eon if the failsafe hadn't been deactivated.{{Refn|[[:File:Failsafe Could Control Eon Transformation.png]]|name=eoncont|group = DR}}

